{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544645-mystery-cults-and-darkness","id":1544645,"title":"Mystery Cults and \"Darkness\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-24T05:49:45-07:00","id":1544645,"title":"Mystery Cults and \"Darkness\"","content":"So I have a player who is a Silver Ladder mage. 1 dot in Order Status, 5 dots in Mystery Cult Influence - so low level within the caucus, but super important to this cult. I understand the mechanics of what he wants, but I've been thinking about flavor and tone the past few days. <br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness is supposed to be &quot;like the real world, but darker&quot;. And one of the things I appreciate about the game is the relative realism of the setting. In the real world, cults can get quite dark indeed. I'm just trying to imagine what this mystery cult is like from the perspective of an NPC the player's mage is interacting with. <br /> <br /> In the real world, the deeper you get into a cult, the more likely it is to involve financial loss, risk of public shaming, or worse, kidnapping, confinement, slavery, human trafficking, physical and sexual abuse. I'm pretty sure neither the player or I are interested in getting that dark. But I also want to maintain an element of realism with touches of creepy spookiness which fits the overall tone of CoD and MtAw.<br /> <br /> I'm interested in how other Storytellers and players have handled this element of Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T09:37:11-07:00","id":1544656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544645-mystery-cults-and-darkness#post1544645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the real world, the deeper you get into a cult, the more likely it is to involve financial loss, risk of public shaming, or worse, kidnapping, confinement, slavery, human trafficking, physical and sexual abuse. I'm pretty sure neither the player or I are interested in getting that dark. But I also want to maintain an element of realism with touches of creepy spookiness which fits the overall tone of CoD and MtAw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, why not run simply cult as 'love bombing &lt;&lt;true family&gt;&gt;'? Hippies communes of 1960s were also cults - but they did not even came close to the true dark elements of cults 'subculture'. Being more positive did not change the fact that people left their lives to live with total strangers, under 'alien' to 'normal people' morality takes.<br /> <br /> Remember also that Silver Ladder promotes paternal take to everything - from magic to social hierarchy. <i>'Of course Tearchs know better how you should stir you life. They are SOOOO great life coaches in the end...'</i><br /> <br /> And, yes, modern life coaches are mini-cults also, in the end. \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-24-2024, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T11:26:51-07:00","id":1544663,"title":"","content":"I would point out that &quot;Mystery Cult&quot; is just used as a generic term for any secretive group with some level of engagement with or connection to the supernatural weirdness of the setting, rather than to specifically reference high control groups based around charismatic narcissists. <br /> <br /> Your average mystery cult more closely resembles a chapter of the Freemasons (and some conspiracy theories attributed to them) rather than NXIVM.<br /> <br /> In terms of the ones connected to the Awakened in particular, you need to think about what the motives of mages are in gathering such groups. While the occasional one who wants to gratify themselves by setting up like a living god is not non-existent, the networks built and maintained by the Orders as a whole are generally concerned with being a means to gather and exert influence, investigate Mysteries, and attempt to direct know the members of that group engage with occult knowledge in accordance with ideology. The kind of abuse you're talking about is not unknown in the Silver Ladder Cryptopoly, but it's the kind of thing somebody has to keep hidden from the caucus lest they be deemed the wrong kind of thearch and punished accordingly.<br /> <br /> That's not to say mystery cults under the Awakened aren't subject to their own kind of abuse. Look at one of the sample groups from the corebook, the Guild. A network of people through an MMORPG isn't exactly the best way to traffic and sexually abuse people, but it's still a group being utilised in a Free Council experiment that they did not consent to. Between that and how the members might be directed towards doing things that may be hazardous or traumatic to them (especially considering that being Sleepers means they still suffer breaking points to Integrity for supernatural encounters), there's still a lot that can be morally dubious to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T12:35:32-07:00","id":1544668,"title":"","content":"I guess there is a larger philosophical question of to what extent mages in MtAw are &quot;baddies&quot;. The overarching theme of the game is that even good intentions, ruthlessly pursued to the point of obsession, can lead to bad results. Personal horror is somewhat downplayed in CoD games as compared to WoD, but it's still in the DNA of the games, especially in the integrity/wisdom mechanic. Lovecraft's Charles Dexter Ward is just your average Mysterium Moros in game terms.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that the Freemasons were entirely harmless in their Victorian heyday. There is a spectrum between like Charles Portis' <i>\u200bMasters of Atlantis</i> and Moore and Campbell's <i>From Hell.</i> Or think of the various mystery cults represented in the Sherlock Homes stories. I remember when I was 10 reading &quot;The Five Orange Pips&quot; and being terrified that the Klu Klux Klan was going to murder me. My mom had to patiently explain that it was extremely unlikely that the Klan was going to come after a white kid living in the suburbs.<br /> <br /> Not to tip my hand too much to coming attractions for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>, but even in the 60s, for every Ken Kesey and the Merry Pranksters or Robert Anton Wilson and Discordians there was a Charles Manson and the Family or Jim Jones and the People's Temple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T13:33:51-07:00","id":1544678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544645-mystery-cults-and-darkness?p=1544668#post1544668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess there is a larger philosophical question of to what extent mages in MtAw are &quot;baddies&quot;. The overarching theme of the game is that even good intentions, ruthlessly pursued to the point of obsession, can lead to bad results. Personal horror is somewhat downplayed in CoD games as compared to WoD, but it's still in the DNA of the games, especially in the integrity/wisdom mechanic. Lovecraft's Charles Dexter Ward is just your average Mysterium Moros in game terms.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that the Freemasons were entirely harmless in their Victorian heyday. There is a spectrum between like Charles Portis' <i>Masters of Atlantis</i> and Moore and Campbell's <i>From Hell.</i> Or think of the various mystery cults represented in the Sherlock Homes stories. I remember when I was 10 reading &quot;The Five Orange Pips&quot; and being terrified that the Klu Klux Klan was going to murder me. My mom had to patiently explain that it was extremely unlikely that the Klan was going to come after a white kid living in the suburbs.<br /> <br /> Not to tip my hand too much to coming attractions for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>, but even in the 60s, for every Ken Kesey and the Merry Pranksters or Robert Anton Wilson and Discordians there was a Charles Manson and the Family or Jim Jones and the People's Temple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, mages <i>are</i> monsters prone to being blinded by their idealism (which is literally it's own world) to the consequences of the real, so yeah, even the Pentacle are *baddies*, of the &quot;the road to hell on earth is paved with good intentions&quot; sort. There's also <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497002-lex-magica-orders-consilia-and-not-behaving-like-seers\">this thread</a> on the subject. <br /> <br /> The big things, as this thread are concerned, are a) what all are your players comfortable with and have consented to to having as part of the game, b) keep in mind that the cult-like abuses you're exploring are more likely to manifest in Awakened abuses of Sleepers rather than strictly Awakened-on-Awakened abuses, with the caveat of c) Awakening is an allegory of the 1% and how their power tends to excuse their abuses as far as society goes, so do with that what you will.<br /> <br /> A lot of answering the specifics of this thread will depends mostly on A, mind. Like, the Precept of Hubris(Secrecy in 1st Edition, if you also want to get way darker about it) basically is supposed to cover the violations of individual's wholeness and autonomy, but when you're dealing with cosmic crimes against humanity and nature, if you want to explore a story where some mages enjoy a little date rape as a treat in contrast to that and how that contrast basically means no one does anything about it, there's room for that story-but it had better be a story everyone's interested in exploring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T14:49:42-07:00","id":1544685,"title":"","content":"Well, I asked them, obviously. And they said that they were pretty open. But I get the sense that most of the players prefer a lighter shade of darkness in the game setting. <br /> <br /> Having said that, if a player puts <i>Mystery Cult Influence 5</i> on their character sheet, and says that it is a cult that manipulates sleeper's dreams, then as an ST I have to figure out how to tell a story with that. And using the Mind Arcanum to muck around in someone's Oneiros seems pretty dark to me, even if the intention is to elicit an Awakening and fight the Lie.<br /> <br /> Sometimes players ask for something, but they don't really mean it. Like &quot;I want to play a Mammon Seer and be rich and powerful AF&quot; and then you're like &quot;OK. Bribe a city council to evict hundreds of poor people from their apartment complex.&quot; And the player is like &quot;oh...nvr mind.&quot;<br /> <br /> But to return to the thread topic, how have you seen Mystery Cults role played in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T15:42:24-07:00","id":1544687,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Mystery Cult shapes dreams to recreate memories from mages, designing dream scenarios that say &quot;you cannot unsee any of this, now what ?&quot;. Since the leader is an Acanthus, it could all be about Choice and Consequences, if you choose to investigate, decide to do something, now you need to be smart about it.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Sleepwalkers&quot; relive them , learn new skills for the next chapter and eventually, they may start noticing the signs of the supernatural in everyday life. The curiosity is there, the drive is balanced by intelligence, but they never saw the supernatural in the flesh. When they do, maybe the Watchtowers would intervene, although the mages running the Cryptopoly would probably keep an eye out for any dangerously reckless actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T18:39:02-07:00","id":1544699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544645-mystery-cults-and-darkness?p=1544678#post1544678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, mages <i>are</i> monsters...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly. Well we will see what happens in the story. Check us out in Play-by-Post if you want.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T19:44:20-07:00","id":1544702,"title":"","content":"<i>'Road to hell is paved with good intentions'</i> - for me players that are not accepting the darker side effects of their actions consequences are not playing 'proper <b>MtAw</b>'. But maybe I'm biased from years of running this game, almost never playing as player myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-25-2024, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T21:22:37-07:00","id":1544704,"title":"","content":"&quot;The good ended happily, and the bad unhappily. That is what fiction means.&quot; - Miss Prism, <i>The Importance of Being Earnest</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T04:01:52-07:00","id":1544716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544645-mystery-cults-and-darkness?p=1544685#post1544685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how have you seen Mystery Cults role played in your games?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? Not that much. My problem is that for mages, cults just don't seem that useful compared to an informal network of personal contacts. Even stuff like the Labyrinth or the Cryptopoly seem like they'd be much easier to run on an informal ad hoc basis.<br /> <br /> A mystery cult makes more sense to me where it's a pre-existing group of people who have rallied around some kind of supernatural thing. Then the mage comes along to get their claws in whatever mystery the cult have discovered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T05:06:37-07:00","id":1544717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544645-mystery-cults-and-darkness?p=1544716#post1544716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly? Not that much. My problem is that for mages, cults just don't seem that useful compared to an informal network of personal contacts. Even stuff like the Labyrinth or the Cryptopoly seem like they'd be much easier to run on an informal ad hoc basis.<br /> <br /> A mystery cult makes more sense to me where it's a pre-existing group of people who have rallied around some kind of supernatural thing. Then the mage comes along to get their claws in whatever mystery the cult have discovered.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually really helpful. <br /> <br /> Although the counter argument is that mystery cults are a big part of the flavor of the source books, and that not enough players play characters that align with the game setting as written","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T08:58:51-07:00","id":1544728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544645-mystery-cults-and-darkness?p=1544668#post1544668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure that the Freemasons were entirely harmless in their Victorian heyday.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that I said the real or conspiracy theory version of them was even slightly harmless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a spectrum between like Charles Portis' <i>Masters of Atlantis</i> and Moore and Campbell's <i>From Hell.</i> Or think of the various mystery cults represented in the Sherlock Homes stories. I remember when I was 10 reading &quot;The Five Orange Pips&quot; and being terrified that the Klu Klux Klan was going to murder me. My mom had to patiently explain that it was extremely unlikely that the Klan was going to come after a white kid living in the suburbs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do the Ku Klux Klan do the kinds of things you were talking about in the original post to which I was responding, or do they hurt people outside of their group?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T10:00:19-07:00","id":1544737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544645-mystery-cults-and-darkness?p=1544717#post1544717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually really helpful.<br /> <br /> Although the counter argument is that mystery cults are a big part of the flavor of the source books, and that not enough players play characters that align with the game setting as written</div> </div> </div> </div>I used a similar idea when writing the <i>Navis Polaris</i> Mystery Cult. People on the outside and initiates see it as some kind of secret society for current and future entrepreneurs. But those who delve deeper see it as explorers of the Mysteries of rewriting one's fortune through business, allowing members to benefit from trading with the denizens of the secret world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}